---
id: org.dxos.plugin.brain
name: BrainPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

The Facts layer for Composer: operations and surfaces over the RDF `Fact` tuples (subject /
predicate / object with factuality, attribution, and provenance) that the space's agents know.

The plugin keeps no fact store of its own. Facts live in each agent's brain (`BrainService` from
`plugin-agent`, one store per agent): `AnalyzeMailbox` writes a mailbox's facts into the brain of the
agent it is given, and the read operations query the brains of every agent in the space, each fact
once. In the client that brain is plugin-agent's in-memory `BrainMemory`, so only facts of agents
hosted in this app are visible here; an EDGE-hosted agent's brain is not reached (roadmap).

On top of the agents' brains, the plugin contributes:

- Two visible operations, `QueryFacts` and `SummarizeSubject`, exposed to the assistant through the
  `org.dxos.skill.brain` skill. Skill instructions describe HOW to use the tools (entity-slug
  conventions, confidence filtering, iterative narrowing) — task-specific behavior lives in the
  operations themselves.
- A `FactsCompanion` surface rendering the plugin's `FactViewer` component over the
  facts the space's agents know (polled through `ListFacts`) as a companion to article subjects,
  with an entity/predicate filter and an empty state when no facts relate to the subject.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`   |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |

## Types

```mdl
type Fact
  desc: |
    Defined in @dxos/pipeline-rdf (not re-declared here). An attributed RDF assertion:
    { id, assertion: { subject: Term, predicate, object: Term }, factuality, attribution,
    recordedAt, extractor, sourceHash }. Terms are { entity, label? } | { literal }.
```

```mdl
type SemanticQueryInput
  desc: |
    The structured (browser-safe) query surface over the triple store. Mirrors
    SemanticQuery from @dxos/pipeline-rdf; no raw SPARQL is exposed to the LLM.
  fields:
    subjectEntity?: string     # Entity slug the fact's subject must match
    predicate?: string         # Exact predicate string
    entity?: string            # Entity slug appearing as subject OR object
    source?: string            # Source DXN the fact was extracted from
    minConfidence?: number     # 0..1 lower bound on factuality confidence
    limit?: number             # Maximum facts returned (default 50)
```

```mdl
type CompactFact
  desc: |
    LLM-facing rendering of a Fact: one line per fact, sized for tool-result context.
    Factuality is the FactBank code (CT+, PR-, ...); date is recordedAt (YYYY-MM-DD).
  fields:
    id: string
    subject: string            # Display label (or slug) of the subject term
    predicate: string
    object: string             # Display label (or slug) / literal of the object term
    factuality: string
    confidence?: number
    date: string
    source: string             # Source DXN
```

```mdl
type SummaryResult
  desc: Output of SummarizeSubject.
  fields:
    summary: string            # Grounded prose summary citing fact ids
    factCount: number          # Number of facts the summary drew from
```

## Operations

```mdl
op queryFacts
  key: org.dxos.operation.brain.queryFacts
  desc: |
    Runs a structured query against the brains of the space's agents and returns compact
    facts for LLM consumption. Visible; listed as a tool of the brain skill.
  input:
    query: SemanticQueryInput
  output: { facts: CompactFact[] }
  requires: [Database, BrainService]
  effects: [brain:read]
  errors:
    BrainError: an agent's brain refused the query or could not be reached
```

```mdl
op summarizeSubject
  key: org.dxos.operation.brain.summarizeSubject
  desc: |
    Queries all facts mentioning the subject (as subject-entity and as object entity),
    then prompts the LLM to compose a grounded summary that cites fact ids and respects
    factuality codes (uncertain facts are hedged, negated facts stated as such).
    Visible; listed as a tool of the brain skill.
  input:
    subject: string            # Entity slug or label (normalized to slug before query)
    focus?: string             # Optional angle, e.g. "commitments", "recent activity"
  output: SummaryResult
  requires: [Database, BrainService, AiService]
  effects: [brain:read, llm]
  errors:
    BrainError: an agent's brain refused the query or could not be reached
  note: Returns { summary: '', factCount: 0 } when no facts match; never invents content.
```

```mdl
op analyzeMailbox
  key: org.dxos.operation.brain.analyzeMailbox
  desc: |
    Cursored fact extraction over a mailbox feed into the named agent's brain. Facts are
    pushed store-only, so bulk ingestion wakes none of the agent's subscriptions.
  input:
    mailbox: Ref<Mailbox>
    agent?: Ref<Agent>         # Required; optional in the schema so a missing one is a typed error
    pageSize?: number
  output: { processed: number, facts: number }
  requires: [AiService, Database, BrainService, TraceService]
  effects: [brain:write, echo:write, llm]
  errors:
    AgentRequiredError: no agent was given
  note: |
    The mailbox processor and the Mailbox Facts template pass the space's only agent; with
    none or several the processor skips the pass and the template's routine has no agent.
```

```mdl
op listFacts
  key: org.dxos.operation.brain.listFacts
  desc: Every fact the brains of the space's agents hold, each once. Read by FactsCompanion.
  output: { facts: Fact[] }
  requires: [Database, BrainService]
  effects: [brain:read]
```

## Components

```mdl
component FactsCompanion
  desc: |
    Companion surface over an article subject rendering the space's facts via the FactViewer
    component (src/components/FactViewer, exported via ./components).
    Facts are read through ListFacts, re-read every few seconds (the brain has no change
    feed). v0 shows all facts of the space's agents with FactViewer's text filter;
    subject-scoped filtering by source DXN is roadmap.
  props:
    subject: Obj.Any           # The companioned ECHO object
  state:
    facts: Fact[]              # Loaded through ListFacts; polled
    filter: string             # Entity/predicate text filter (FactViewer built-in)
  slots: {}
  emits: {}
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Facts live in the agents' brains

  req F-1.1:
    when: the plugin activates
    then: it contributes no fact store; its operations declare BrainService

  req F-1.2:
    when: AnalyzeMailbox runs without an agent
    then: it fails with AgentRequiredError before reading the mailbox

  req F-1.3:
    when: AnalyzeMailbox runs with an agent
    then: the facts land in that agent's brain, stored without waking its subscriptions

  req F-1.4:
    when: the agent is hosted on EDGE
    then: the facts reach EDGE's brain, which its Knowledge panel reads
    tags: [roadmap]
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Assistant access via the brain skill

  req F-2.1:
    when: the plugin activates
    then: the org.dxos.skill.brain skill is contributed with tools QueryFacts and
          SummarizeSubject

  req F-2.2:
    when: the skill instructions are rendered
    then: they describe tool usage only (slug conventions, confidence filtering,
          iterative narrowing); no task-specific recipes

  req F-2.3:
    when: the assistant invokes QueryFacts
    then: results are compact single-line facts bounded by limit (default 50)
```

```mdl
feat F-3: FactViewer companion surface

  req F-3.1:
    when: an article subject is companioned in a space with an agent
    then: the FactsCompanion surface is available and renders FactViewer over the
          space's facts

  req F-3.2:
    when: the space's agents know no facts
    then: an empty state is shown (no error)
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Readers query the agents' brains

  req F-4.1:
    when: QueryFacts, SummarizeSubject or GenerateReply reads facts
    then: it queries the brain of every agent in the space and keeps each fact once
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Facts written through the brain
  given: a mailbox feed and an agent with an in-memory brain
  when: the fact pipeline runs into that agent's brain
  then:
    - the agent's brain holds the extracted facts
    - none of the agent's subscriptions woke
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: QueryFacts returns matching facts
  given: an agent whose in-memory brain holds facts about alice (subject) and acme (object)
  when: QueryFacts runs with { entity: 'alice' } and with { minConfidence: 0.9 }
  then:
    - the entity query returns facts where alice is subject or object
    - the confidence query excludes facts below the bound
    - results are CompactFact-shaped and bounded by limit
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: SummarizeSubject grounds on facts
  given: an agent whose in-memory brain holds facts about a person, and a stub LLM
  when: SummarizeSubject runs with that subject
  then:
    - factCount equals the number of matched facts
    - the summary cites at least one fact id
    - with an unknown subject: summary is empty and factCount is 0
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: FactsCompanion rendering
  given: a space agent whose brain holds facts (storybook)
  when: FactsCompanion renders over a subject
  then:
    - FactViewer shows the facts grouped by subject
    - with an empty brain the empty state renders
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: Analyze → query integration
  given: a mailbox feed with messages and a space agent
  when: AnalyzeMailbox runs for that agent, then QueryFacts for a participant entity
  then: facts extracted from the messages are returned
```

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

This plugin has no create operation of its own — facts land in an agent's brain via pipelines
(`AnalyzeMailbox`, the agent's own reading), never through a user gesture this plugin owns — so there is
nothing for `before`/`test` to create and nothing for `after` to undo. `queryFacts` and
`summarizeSubject` are both agent-invocable read operations (`op@1.1`, keys below).

```mdl
test QA-1: Query and summarize facts already in the store
  desc: The plugin's own surface — QueryFacts and SummarizeSubject against a space agent's pre-populated brain.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-2.1, F-2.3, F-3.1, T-2, T-3]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open whose agent's brain already holds facts about entity "alice-smith" —
      seeded by a prior AnalyzeMailbox run (see F-1.3); this plugin has no operation that creates
      a fact itself
  steps:
    - name: Query facts about the entity
      do: (no direct UI for a structured query — this is the assistant path; a human instead opens
        the FactsCompanion below and types "alice-smith" into its filter)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.brain.queryFacts { entity: "alice-smith" }
      capture: queried
      expect: every returned fact has "alice-smith" as its subject or object entity, bounded by
        the default limit of 50
      assert: return $result.facts.length > 0 && $result.facts.every((f) => f.subject.includes('alice') || f.object.includes('alice'));
    - name: Summarize the entity
      do: (assistant path only — ask the assistant "summarize alice-smith")
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.brain.summarizeSubject { subject: "alice-smith" }
      expect: a grounded summary is returned that cites at least one fact id, with factCount > 0
      assert: return $result.factCount > 0 && $result.summary.length > 0;
    - name: Open the FactsCompanion
      do: Companion an object touched by the seeded facts (e.g. the enriched mailbox message) and
        open its Facts companion panel.
      expect: FactViewer lists the space's facts, filterable by entity/predicate text
      note: NO `invoke` — FactsCompanion is a read-only React surface, not backed by an operation.
```

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap        # name[?]: TypeExpr  (# inline comment)
    literals?: UnionList     # a | b | c
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap            # external inputs (immutable inside component)
    state?: FieldMap            # internal reactive state
    slots?: FieldMap            # named ReactNode injection points
    actions?: ActionMap         # methods the component exposes or handles
    emits?: EventMap            # events the component raises to its parent
    layout?: CodeBlock          # ASCII sketch of visual structure (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap            # named input parameters
    output?: TypeExpr           # return type
    errors?: ErrorMap           # name: Prose  (when this error occurs)
    effects?: EffectList        # echo:read | echo:write | http | fs | ...
    requires?: ServiceList      # injected service dependencies
    note?: Prose                # implementation guidance (non-normative)
```
